---
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro'
import Link from '@/components/Link.astro'
import PageHead from '@/components/PageHead.astro'
import { buttonVariants } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { SITE, SOCIAL_LINKS } from '@/consts'
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'

const email = SOCIAL_LINKS.find((link) => link.label === 'Email')
const personSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Andrew Raisbeck',
  url: SITE.href,
  jobTitle: 'Enterprise developer and IBM Maximo/MAS specialist',
  description:
    'Enterprise application development, IBM Maximo/MAS, systems integration and application reliability for public-sector water and wastewater operations.',
}
---

<Layout class="max-w-3xl">
  <PageHead slot="head" title="About" />
  <script
    is:inline
    type="application/ld+json"
    set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)}
  />
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About', icon: 'lucide:user' }]} />

  <section aria-labelledby="about-heading" class="space-y-10 pb-8">
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <h1 id="about-heading" class="text-3xl font-bold md:text-4xl">
        About me
      </h1>
      <p class="text-primary text-lg font-medium">Andrew Raisbeck</p>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
        I’m an enterprise developer and IBM Maximo/MAS specialist. I build
        applications and integrations for public-sector water and wastewater
        operations, with a focus on making everyday work easier and keeping
        essential systems reliable.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        At York Region, I work across application development, platform
        administration, support and systems integration. I work directly with
        operations staff and other stakeholders to understand their
        requirements, then carry that work through development, deployment,
        training and ongoing support.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="development-heading" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 id="development-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold">
        Application development and reliability
      </h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        I developed eLogbook, a Java Struts/Spring extension to EZMaxMobile that
        lets water and wastewater staff maintain facility logbooks both
        centrally and in the field. I also rebuilt the logbook application using
        IBM Maximo Mobile’s React-based framework. My independent consulting
        work includes React web applications and Visual Basic desktop tools.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        Beyond application code, I introduced Azure DevOps CI/CD pipelines that
        eliminated manual deployment errors and cut releases from several hours
        to 30–40 minutes. I implemented Prometheus and Grafana monitoring for
        Maximo and EZMaxMobile on WebSphere, and developed JUnit load tests that
        simulated hundreds of authenticated users. Together, the monitoring and
        load testing helped identify and eliminate the source of recurring Java
        crashes and the downtime they caused.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="maximo-heading" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 id="maximo-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold">
        Maximo applications, integrations and modernization
      </h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        My Maximo work includes custom on-call scheduling and absence request
        applications, extending Graphical Resource View to replace an Oracle
        APEX scheduling system, and standardizing laboratory water sample
        results with automated unit conversion, anomaly detection and error
        reporting. Scheduling automation reduced the total time spent building
        and maintaining staff schedules by 80–90%.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        I build integrations using Maximo enterprise services, SSIS, REST APIs
        and Denodo middleware. These connect MAS with on-premises PeopleSoft
        data and a data warehouse supporting Power BI dashboards. I also
        maintain bidirectional GIS integration and have set up a Historian API
        pilot to update Maximo asset runtime meters from SCADA data for
        preventive and predictive maintenance.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        During a concurrent Acting Program Manager assignment, I led a small
        specialist team through a Maximo 7.6.x to MAS 9.1 upgrade, a move from
        WebSphere to Red Hat OpenShift and a cloud migration in just over six
        months. Separately, my analysis of concurrent login and application
        usage, security group optimization and transition to IBM App Points
        produced more than CAD $1.2 million in projected licensing savings over
        10 years.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="approach-heading" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 id="approach-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold">How I work</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        Working in the public sector has taught me to make practical decisions
        within limited budgets and existing infrastructure. I’m comfortable
        working on established Java systems as well as newer React applications,
        and I pay attention to what happens after a release: how staff use an
        application, how it behaves under load and how the team will maintain
        it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        I’ve presented at the Canadian Maximo User Group in Toronto and enjoy
        sharing what I learn. Outside work, I spend time on open-source tools,
        AI and self-hosting projects. I also enjoy weightlifting, running,
        camping and baseball.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      aria-labelledby="connect-heading"
      class="border-border bg-muted/10 space-y-5 rounded-xl border p-5 sm:p-6"
    >
      <h2 id="connect-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold">Let’s talk</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        I’m interested in developer and Maximo specialist roles where I can
        build useful applications, solve integration problems and improve system
        reliability.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <Link
          href="/#maximo-experience"
          class={buttonVariants({ variant: 'outline' })}
        >
          Maximo / MAS experience
        </Link>
        <Link
          href="/#developer-experience"
          class={buttonVariants({ variant: 'outline' })}
        >
          Development experience
        </Link>
        {
          email && (
            <Link
              href={email.href}
              class={buttonVariants({ variant: 'default' })}
            >
              Email me
            </Link>
          )
        }
      </div>
    </section>
  </section>
</Layout>
